# Test: RFC 2516 PPPoE discovery exchange (PADI -> PADO -> PADR -> PADS).
# VALIDATES: PADO carries AC-Name and AC-Cookie (RFC 2516 Section 5.2, 5.5)
# VALIDATES: a PADR with a valid AC-Cookie yields PADS with a non-zero session id
# VALIDATES: a PADR with a forged AC-Cookie gets no PADS (VerifyCookie, cookie.go)
# PREVENTS: an AC that hands out sessions to any PADR, which is the DoS the
# AC-Cookie exists to stop -- delete the VerifyCookie call in handlePADR
# (internal/component/l2tp/pppoe/server.go) and the forged-cookie phase below
# gets a PADS and fails.
#
# The daemon binds AF_PACKET to veth-bng and the client to veth-sub, the two ends
# of one veth pair inside this test's own network namespace, so the frames below
# are real Ethernet frames through the kernel and not a loopback of the encoder.
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw
option=netns-link:name=veth-bng:peer=veth-sub


stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
pppoe {
    enabled true
    ac-name ze-test
    interface veth-bng {
    }
}
EOF_CONF

option=env:var=ze.log.pppoe:value=debug
option=env:var=TEST_IFACE:value=veth-sub

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=config
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test fixture pppoe/basic:timeout=45s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: PADO received
expect=stdout:contains=OK: PADS received
expect=stdout:contains=OK: forged AC-Cookie PADR silently dropped
